-device scsi-hd,drive=disk0 \
--enable-kvm \
--nographic

I have recreated same issue with QEMU master as well as v10.2.2 along 
with edk2-stable202602.

A git bisect on the host kernel identified the following as the first 
bad commit:

88b16bf7bdc507c529a05ccc771a80615caca0e1 is the first bad commit
commit 88b16bf7bdc507c529a05ccc771a80615caca0e1
Author: Sean Christopherson <seanjc@google.com>
Date:   Tue Mar 10 16:48:13 2026 -0700
     KVM: SEV: Lock all vCPUs when synchronzing VMSAs for SNP launch finish


There are no error messages on either the host or guest serial console 
when this happens.

Reverting this commit makes the problem go away.

